    "description": [
        {
            "result": {
                "value": "Source code for OOPS! (OntOlogy Pitfall Scanner!) application",
                "type": "String"
            },
            "confidence": 1,
            "technique": "GitHub_API"
        },
        {
            "result": {
                "value": "OOPS+ is an extension of the original OOPS! ontology pitfall scanner. The original OOPS! application provides the immediate ontology evaluation report, while OOPS+ adds a second report pipeline for checks that require an LLM.\n\nThe current setup contains two web applications:\n\n- **OOPs**: the regular OOPS! application. It generates the normal report immediately.\n- **OOPsPlus**: the extended application. It processes OOPS+ jobs and generates the LLM-based report.\n\nWhen the user enables OOPS+ in the OOPs web interface, OOPs stores the submitted ontology in a shared analysis directory, creates a job, and publishes it to RabbitMQ. An OOPS+ worker consumes that job, runs the OOPsPlus analysis, writes the generated HTML report, and updates the job status. The OOPS+ report page reads that status and displays the report when it is ready.\n",
                "type": "Text_excerpt",
                "original_header": "Description",
                "parent_header": [
                    "OOPS+"
                ]
            },
            "confidence": 1.0,
